 (closure-size-exceeded, computed value, provider-defined attribute, dynamic source) have no obvious member in the existing enum, so an executor cannot know which reason token to emit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f65d4d42536d7d422","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope and mechanics section (abstention list, closure caps) and Registry-access paragraph; AC lines for probe_source and corroborate_diagnostic","norm_id":"nd839dc72f6f1708f","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An agent receives an abstain for a closure-size-exceeded query but the reason token is undefined, so the model cannot distinguish it from a parse failure","probe_source 401 vs 404 vs TLS failure must all be closed abstentions, but the plan does not bind each to a reason token"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that each Terraform abstain arm binds to a named reason from a closed enum, extending grounding.schema.json's abstain_reason with the Terraform-specific members the existing set cannot express (closure-limit, computed-value, provider-defined-attribute, dynamic-source).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name and verify (against --help/docs) the concrete terraform-config-inspect invocation the adapter uses — subcommand, the JSON-output flag, the directory/snapshot input contract, and the actual version-discovery mechanism — classifying each as MATCH/MISMATCH/UNVERIFIED before slice 4 commits.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'its JSON is schema-checked and its absolute path, binary digest, and discoverable version are recorded'","Plan: 'It receives a minimal copied snapshot of approved module files'","T3 empiricism axis (a): OBSERVE flag names from --help, do not infer them from memory or a prior version — flag-level mismatches cause silent runtime failures after ship","terraform-config-inspect is a minimal HashiCorp Go tool; whether it exposes a version flag/field and the exact JSON-emitting invocation are load-bearing but unstated (UNVERIFIED)"],"finding":"The plan depends on terraform-config-inspect's CLI surface (schema-checked JSON output, a 'discoverable version', and copied-snapshot/directory input) but never names the actual invocation flags/subcommand or cites --help/docs; the flag surface and version-discovery are inferred, not observed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2eb2f37c006b0057","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope and mechanics — 'terraform-config-inspect is the only optional executable allowed in V1' bullet; Outcome — corroborate_diagnostic","norm_id":"nf84bd2497fe18ed5","priority":0.088,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Slice 4 wires the adapter with an assumed invocation/flag that the shipped terraform-config-inspect binary does not accept, producing a silent abstain (or parse failure) on every call after ship","The recorded 'discoverable version' field has no source flag on the actual binary, so provenance recording silently degrades"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the corroborate_diagnostic bullet, pin the observed invocation (e.g. `terraform-config-inspect --json <snapshot-dir>`), the JSON schema fields relied on, and how version is discovered; make the slice-4 'live contract canary' the explicit spike that verifies this surface against the real binary before the full adapter lands.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the specific Terraform registry metadata endpoint(s) probe_source queries and confirm the path/response shape and TF_TOKEN auth/scope against the registry API docs (MATCH/MISMATCH/UNVERIFIED).","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.834,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'probe_source: inspect repo-contained local sources and positive registry metadata reachable with existing ambient credentials'","T3 endpoint granularity: the unit is a specific endpoint SURFACE, not the vendor; a new endpoint is a NEW int